{"kind":"event","event_id":7660,"event_uid":"01M2P7YZHBEK25AA79TPRYH3ZN","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":322,"issue_uid":"01M2P7TKPND17DRJK8EPR5DPG8","issue_short_id":"dpg8","actor":"exam:1@run-24","hlc_physical_ms":1789600431659,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"d5b64a0f3f523b4d3a7def925b94196be102141188a2d902212d5f8532be1fb9","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2P7YZHAC3CF4B66NWWY0642","author":"exam:1@run-24","body":"Examiner, round 1. Approach: one file at the Proof `Test:` path `tests/state-exams/set-todo-tags.test.ts` (no EXAM PATHS line, so it lands where the Proof names it), eleven legs (a)-(k), one test per pinned value where a leg says \"one assertion per row\". Following the two precedents this repo already sets: `pin-todo.test.ts` for the namespace import `import * as sd from '../../client/src/storeData'` (a named import of a symbol absent at BASE is one load error for the whole file) and `set-todo-due.test.ts` for the computed-specifier `await import(resolve(ROOT, 'client/src/todoTags.ts'))` inside each test body (the module itself does not exist at BASE). Every fixture read inside a test body; the only module-level read is `readdirSync` of the two snapshot directories, which exist at BASE, so leg (i)'s failing file is the failing test's name. Leg (i) reads the directories rather than pinning a count — the plan's siblings add files to both. Legs (j)/(k) spawn the two `Run:` lines verbatim through `bash -c` from the repository root with a timeout above Bun's 5 s.","created_at":"2026-09-16T23:13:51.658351199Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T23:13:51.659Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7661,"event_uid":"01M2P802N0NSH1BZ3W5A8P956N","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":322,"issue_uid":"01M2P7TKPND17DRJK8EPR5DPG8","issue_short_id":"dpg8","actor":"impl:1@run-24","hlc_physical_ms":1789600467616,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"9cdbcf6697be71ebfcc34f2375443771073edd9b306b9dad2fd41b20d95b21c7","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2P802MYV5PJ35784P9KVDKK","author":"impl:1@run-24","body":"Approach for task 1 (tags cell + tag value + readings):\n\n- `client/src/todoTags.ts`: new, imports nothing (the shape `todoFilter.ts` has). Seven exports: parseTags, normalizeTags, isNormalizedTags, tagsInUse, countTagged, activeTag, hasTag.\n- `client/src/storeData.ts`: `tags: {type: 'string'}` appended to TODO_CELLS (no default), `tag: {type: 'string'}` appended to VALUES_SCHEMA (no default), one INVARIANTS entry appended (never inserted — invariants.test.ts reads INVARIANTS[0]), and setTodoTags/setTagFilter mirroring pinTodo/setFilter.\n- `client/src/DoneCount.tsx`: a fragment — the doneCount span byte for byte as it was, plus `<span id=\"taggedCount\">{tagged} tagged</span>`.\n- `state-exams/expected/two-todos-second-tagged.json`: one line, tables first.\n- `tests/state-exams/set-filter.test.ts` leg (d): the getValuesSchemaJson pin loosened to the `filter` entry alone, never re-pinned to the new two-entry literal.\n\nThe linter's four test files are in Files in case a pin goes red; I will run them first and only loosen what actually fires.","created_at":"2026-09-16T23:14:27.614555397Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T23:14:27.616Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":7676,"event_uid":"01M2P8H0VZA4G3572D75KY1RZ6","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":322,"issue_uid":"01M2P7TKPND17DRJK8EPR5DPG8","issue_short_id":"dpg8","actor":"exam:1@run-24","hlc_physical_ms":1789601022847,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"6cf0e64de4e997065ab32114a7e3dcb7ce042ace21f15a4dcd6eeeafd895fc84","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2P8H0VYHPX5HG5GNPTDJZB4","author":"exam:1@run-24","body":"Examiner, round 1 — exam handed in at `tests/state-exams/set-todo-tags.test.ts`, all eleven legs (a)-(k) encoded, nothing unsatisfiable. Red at BASE: 45 fail / 25 pass over 70 tests, and every red reads as the absent implementation — 20 `Cannot find module client/src/todoTags.ts`, 11 `typeof sd.setTodoTags|setTagFilter` not a function, 6 the `INVARIANTS` entry not found by its message, 5 the absent `tags`/`tag` schema entries and the absent `#taggedCount`, 2 the absent `state-exams/expected/two-todos-second-tagged.json`, 1 the state exam's own action. The 25 that pass are the 23 BASE snapshots round-tripping (leg (i)), `INVARIANTS[0].message` still the linter's entry, and the `<span id=\\\"doneCount\\\">0 of 2 done</span>` substring already in both markups — that last one is asserted so that a later change to that span is this exam's red too.\n\nFour readings a later session would otherwise reconstruct:\n\n1. Leg (k) is red at BASE *transitively*, and that is not a defect. This exam file names an expected file the implementer has yet to create, so `bun run lint:state`'s `views` rule reports `tests/state-exams/set-todo-tags.test.ts -> state-exams/expected/two-todos-second-tagged.json`; that turns `packages/tinyapp-lint/test/views.test.ts` red (leg (j)) and, through its own leg (l), `tests/state-exams/set-filter.test.ts` red (leg (k)). Creating `state-exams/expected/two-todos-second-tagged.json` clears both. The file is in the task's own Create list, so it is a deliverable and not a fixture the exam forgot to write.\n\n2. Leg (i) reads `state-exams/seeds` and `state-exams/expected` with `readdirSync` and pins no count of either — M9's \"five seeds and fifteen expected states\" is stale against BASE (six and seventeen) and the two tasks running beside this one add to both. Nothing else here pins a count either: no callback list, no snapshot count, no `INVARIANTS` length. M7's entry is found by its message and never by its index, and `INVARIANTS[0]` is asserted by the message it carries. This task's own expected file also gets one named round-trip test beside the walk, so a run in which it is simply missing says so rather than quietly listing one file fewer.\n\n3. `storeData.ts` is reached by namespace import (`import * as sd`) and `todoTags.ts` by computed-specifier `await import(resolve(ROOT, 'client/src/todoTags.ts'))` inside each test body — the precedents `pin-todo.test.ts` and `set-todo-due.test.ts` set. Both are load-bearing: a static import of an absent module or an absent named export is one red for the whole file, and every leg would then report that import instead of the clause it is about.\n\n4. M5's three refused strings (`'home,urgent'`, `' home'`, `'Home '`) are each measured from a store that has already had `setTagFilter(store, 'home')` applied, which is M5's own \"then\". That makes the assertion stronger than a fresh store would: a refused string neither replaces a chosen filter nor clears it. Each case is its own test with its own store, so a red names the string.","created_at":"2026-09-16T23:23:42.846355729Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T23:23:42.847Z"}
